      "definition": "(1) \"Within a township\" includes all land, including, but not limited to, any part of any municipal corporation, that is physically located within the territorial boundaries of that township, whether or not that land or municipal corporation is governmentally a part of the township.",
      "id": "1901.02-within-a-township",
      "normalized": "within a township",
      "scope": "(C) As used in this section:",
      "section": "1901.02",
      "source_title": "Section 1901.02 - Jurisdiction of municipal courts.",
      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-1901.02",
      "term": "Within a township"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(2) \"Within a municipal corporation\" includes all land within the territorial boundaries of the municipal corporation and any townships that are coextensive with the municipal corporation.\n\nLast updated August 28, 2024 at 1:42 PM",
